.TH PTY_SCREEN_COMPARE 3 2026-10-03 "libptytest 0.1" "libptytest Manual"
.SH NAME
pty_screen_compare, pty_screen_dump \- compare the whole screen, cell for
cell; print it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <ptytest.h>
.PP
.BI "int pty_screen_compare(PtySession *" s ", const char *const " expected "[],"
.BI "                       char *" report ", size_t " report_size );
.BI "void pty_screen_dump(PtySession *" s ", FILE *" fp );
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR pty_screen_compare ()
compares every row of the screen with the expected picture.
.I expected
is a NULL-terminated array of UTF-8 strings, one per row from the top; rows
past the end of the array are expected to be blank, so a stray line at the
bottom of the screen is a difference.
Within a row, trailing blanks are not significant and everything else is:
a character one column to the left or right, a missing border character,
a truncated word.
A wide character occupies two columns of the screen and is written once in
the expected string.
.PP
Attributes and colours are not part of the comparison; check the cells
that carry them with
.BR pty_cell_attr (3),
.BR pty_cell_fg (3)
and
.BR pty_cell_bg (3).
.PP
If
.I report
is not NULL it receives, for every differing row, the row number, the
column of the first difference, and both versions of the row framed with
\(oq|\(cq.
It is always NUL-terminated and is truncated to
.IR report_size .
.PP
.BR pty_screen_dump ()
prints the screen to
.IR fp ,
untrimmed and framed, with row numbers, a column ruler and the cursor
position \(em the thing to print when an assertion fails.
.SH RETURN VALUE
.BR pty_screen_compare ()
returns 0 if the screen matches, the number of differing rows otherwise,
and \-1 if
.I expected
has more rows than the screen or an argument is NULL.
.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
const char *const expected[] = {
    "┌ Inbox ─────────────┐",
    "│> Meeting moved     │",
    "│  Invoice 2026\-09   │",
    "└────────────────────┘",
    NULL
};
char report[4096];
if (pty_screen_compare(s, expected, report, sizeof(report)) != 0) {
    fputs(report, stdout);
    pty_screen_dump(s, stdout);
}
.EE
.PP
A report looks like this:
.PP
.EX
row  1 differs at col 3
  expected |│> Meeting moved     │|
  actual   |│ > Meeting moved    │|
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pty_assert (3),
.BR pty_row_text (3),
.BR pty_cell_text (3)
